memory/decisions/

# Generated artifact, not hand-edited: scripts/build-dogfood-coverage.py writes
# it with json.dumps(indent=2), which always expands short arrays; prettier
# collapses them. Two writers, two formats, so EVERY run of
# check-req-coverage.py left a ~1,700-line diff that was 100% formatting
# (MHQ-734). That churn is not cosmetic — it hid a real staleness bug once
# (ING-T3-03 missing a test file, invisible inside the noise) and manufactured
# a false one later, when the diff was read as artifact rot that did not exist.
# Letting json.dumps be canonical makes the writer's own "unchanged" check
# effective, so a clean tree stays clean.
engineering/dogfood-coverage.json
